\ Fast gate-position ownership checks: none makes a full sauce.
\ The four zero crossings must choose their outgoing signed gap
\ without ever selecting invalid gap index 0. Coordinates and index
\ commits are separately protected against a failed interval.
\ The heavy cross-zero arithmetic test is optional.

The tested wide gate index is a wide signed day.
The tested gate magnitude is a wide quantity.

To check wide gate gap ownership:
  Begin a wide gate traversal.
  Put "1" into the tested gate magnitude.
  Set the current wide gate's index from the tested gate magnitude given -1.
  Prepare a wide forward gate movement.
  If the wide gate movement's next index's polarity is not 0,
    put "Wide gate -1 did not move next to zero." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide gate movement's gap index's polarity is not -1,
    put "Crossing negative gate -1 failed to retain its gap." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide gate movement's gap index's magnitude is not "1",
    put "The negative gap index has an incorrect magnitude." into the check report; exit.
  Put "0" into the tested gate magnitude.
  Set the current wide gate's index from the tested gate magnitude given 0.
  Prepare a wide forward gate movement.
  If the wide gate movement's gap index's polarity is not 1,
    put "Moving from zero to positive one selected a nonpositive gap." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide gate movement's gap index's magnitude is not "1",
    put "Moving from zero to positive one selected the wrong gap." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1" into the tested gate magnitude.
  Set the current wide gate's index from the tested gate magnitude given 1.
  Prepare a wide backward gate movement.
  If the wide gate movement's next index's polarity is not 0,
    put "Backward positive one did not reach zero." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide gate movement's gap index's polarity is not 1,
    put "Backward positive crossing selected a negative gap." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide gate movement's gap index's magnitude is not "1",
    put "Backward positive crossing selected the wrong gap." into the check report; exit.
  Put "0" into the tested gate magnitude.
  Set the current wide gate's index from the tested gate magnitude given 0.
  Prepare a wide backward gate movement.
  If the wide gate movement's next index's polarity is not -1,
    put "Backward movement from zero did not reach minus one." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide gate movement's gap index's polarity is not -1,
    put "Backward movement from zero used the wrong signed gap." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide gate movement's gap index's magnitude is not "1",
    put "Backward movement from zero used the wrong gap magnitude." into the check report; exit.

To check blocked wide gate movements:
  Begin a wide gate traversal.
  Put 0 into the gate step budget's steps remaining.
  Prepare a wide forward gate movement.
  Commit the prepared wide gate movement.
  If the wide gate movement's succeeded is not 0,
    put "Exhausted wide gate movement was incorrectly committed." into the check report; exit.
  If the current wide gate's index's polarity is not 0,
    put "Blocked wide gate movement changed its index." into the check report; exit.
  If the current wide gate's coordinate's magnitude is not "15055671",
    put "Blocked wide gate movement changed the Foundation coordinate." into the check report; exit.
  Begin a wide gate traversal.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000" into the tested gate magnitude.
  Set the tested wide gate index from the tested gate magnitude given 1.
  Locate a wide gate given the tested wide gate index.
  If the current wide gate's reached is not 0,
    put "A distant wide gate escaped the bounded traversal." into the check report; exit.
  If the current wide gate's index's magnitude is not "0",
    put "A distant rejected gate moved the working index." into the check report; exit.
  If the current wide gate's coordinate's magnitude is not "15055671",
    put "A distant rejected gate moved the Foundation position." into the check report; exit.
  Put "0" into the tested gate magnitude.
  Set the tested wide gate index from the tested gate magnitude given 0.
  Locate a wide gate given the tested wide gate index.
  If the current wide gate's reached is not 1,
    put "The zero gate should remain directly reachable." into the check report; exit.
  If the current wide gate's index's polarity is not 0,
    put "The exact zero gate has a nonzero index." into the check report; exit.

\ Slow integration verifies exact positions using two complete sauces.
To check a wide gate crossing Foundation:
  Begin a wide gate traversal.
  Move to the next positive wide gate.
  If the wide gate movement's succeeded is not 1,
    put "A wide positive gate move failed." into the check report; exit.
  If the current wide gate's coordinate's polarity is not -1,
    put "The first wide positive gate has an incorrect sign." into the check report; exit.
  If the current wide gate's coordinate's magnitude is not "15055326",
    put "The first positive wide gate must be Foundation plus 345 days." into the check report; exit.
  Move to the next negative wide gate.
  If the wide gate movement's succeeded is not 1,
    put "A wide backward gate move failed." into the check report; exit.
  If the current wide gate's coordinate's magnitude is not "15055671",
    put "Returning to Foundation did not undo the first wide gap." into the check report; exit.
